# Every acceptance id in PHASE-1-PLAN.md that this repo's CI reports on, with
# where it's checked: a workflow's name, or "manual" for a check on the NUC.
# Grows stage by stage (ADR-019). test/agentv/report reads this.

S0.1  agentv-iso a tagged release's ISO installs in CI and boots to the TV setup welcome screen
S0.2  manual    the NUC boots from the ISO to the welcome screen, with no boot password (agentv selftest S0.2)
S0.3  manual    NetworkManager brings up the setup hotspot on the NUC's Wi-Fi (agentv selftest S0.3)
S0.4  agentv-iso the AgenTV logo in the installer, boot splash and screensaver; no Omarchy file edited
S0.5  nightly   agentv update moves a box to a newer release in place, with a snapshot in the boot menu
S0.6  sync      a new Omarchy stable tag gets a sync pull request that merges itself only when green
S0.7  nightly   a box holds back a package version until the signed tested.json lists it
S1.1  image     cold boot lands in the TV session on the welcome page, with nothing of Omarchy's desktop in it
S1.2  manual    10 minutes of a streaming service at 720p in the services' Chromium, no stutter, no fan (agentv selftest S1.2)
S1.3  image     TV to Omarchy's desktop and back each take under 10 s
S1.4  agentv-plugin the Back to TV plugin passes omarchy plugin validate (the repo isn't made yet)
S1.5  manual    the TV session check: 60 fps, an app and home again, a toast over a film, Steam in its gamescope (agentv selftest S1.5)
S1.6  image     no window takes the screen unless the daemon puts it in front: a new window, a home screen crash, an update
S2.1  check     a sample app installs from a signed test index, and a tampered index is refused
S2.2  check     agentv app validate rejects a symlink, an unsafe entry path and a third-party agentv.* id
S2.3  check     every tile can be reached with the keyboard alone
S2.4  check     a tile dragged with the mouse lands where it was dropped, and the layout survives a reboot
S2.5  check     a tile resized with +/-, by its corner or from the size bar takes only the sizes its manifest lists
S2.6  check     the tiles it covers move to the next free cells, and a size with no room can't be picked
S2.7  check     no tile shows a tier, and every app's details say who made it
S2.10 manual    the focus glide, hover lift and page transitions at 60 fps on the NUC; reduce motion fades (layer 4 checks the rules)
S2.11 manual    each UI sound within a frame of its action; move at most every 60 ms; Settings → Sound silences them (layer 4 checks the rules)
